							"left": 803,
							"top": 36,
							"width": 312,
							"height": 167,
							"text": "Event-Driven Architecture:\n– Services communicate asynchronously through an EventBus (e.g., RabbitMQ/Kafka).\n– Events such as PetCreated, TaskCreated, TaskDue drive system behavior.\n– Services publish events when state changes, and other services react by subscribing.\n– Enables loose coupling, high scalability, and real-time reactions.\n– Ideal for notifications, scheduling, and asynchronous workflows.\n"
						}
