							"left": 839,
							"top": 48,
							"width": 336,
							"height": 167,
							"text": "Event-Driven Deployment:\n– Services run independently and communicate via a centralized Message Broker.\n– Publish/Subscribe channels carry domain events between services.\n– MessageBroker (e.g., RabbitMQ, Kafka) ensures reliability and decoupling.\n– Services can scale independently and process events asynchronously.\n– Suitable for high-volume notifications, task scheduling, and real-time updates.\n"
						}
					]
